    "https://berufungsportal.uni-frankfurt.de/application?procedure=4C6376C0-C381-9FD9-F03E-9185AFD2DF9A": {
      "title": "specific requirements listed under “Your profile” that are necessary for fulfilling the duties of the professorship.",
      "description": "www.uni-frankfurt.de Goethe University Frankfurt am Main invites applications for the position of in the Institute of Judaic Studies at the Faculty of Linguistics, Cultures, and Arts. This civil servant or public employee position will start as soon as possible. The position is based at the department for Judaic Studies and represents Israel Studies as part of Jewish Studies. Within Israel Studies, a focus on history, culture / literature, religion, or anthropology is expected. The successful candidate will participate in teaching in the Jewish Studies degree programs. They will be responsible for the teaching of both Israel and modern Diaspora Judaism within Jewish Studies, and will align their instruction with both Jewish Studies students and an interdisciplinary audience, with a bridge to Islamic Studies being welcome. The position is directly connected to the LOEWE Center “Dynamics of Religion: Ambivalent Neighborhoods between Judaism, Christianity, and Islam in Historical and Contemporary Configurations,” funded by the HMWK, and is expected to contribute actively to its research through an independent subproject, and if possible, also in teaching. You have extensive research experience in the field of the history and culture of the State of Israel and Israeli society, set against the backdrop of broad expertise in modern Judaism. We expect a research focus that includes, among other things, religious and interreligious aspects of Israeli society and culture (e.g., religious-cultural neighborly relations, religious pluralism in Israeli society, Jewish-Muslim relations, and the tension between religious and secular spheres of society), possibly also extending to religious, cultural, and political neighborly relations in the context of the Middle East. We expect a willingness to actively contribute to the expansion of the LOEWE Center’s research field, including through independent third-party funding initiatives or participation in collaborative projects. International experience is required, as is a readiness to engage in interdisciplinary and collaborative research. Teaching experience and experience in securing third-party funding are desirable. Knowledge of German is advantageous; teaching must be conducted in German after two years at the latest. The employment requirements as defined in § 68 of HessHG apply. Among other things, this includes proof of aptitude for academic work (e.g., a doctorate), additional academic achievements (e.g., a habilitation or equivalent), and the subject- specific requirements listed under “Your profile” that are necessary for fulfilling the duties of the professorship. Goethe University is committed to equal opportunity, family friendliness, and diversity. To strengthen the diversity of perspectives and lived experiences within the university, applications from individuals with a migration background and from members of other groups that have so far been underrepresented are particularly welcome. Applicants with a severe disability, or those legally equivalent, will be given preferential consideration in cases of equal suitability. If women are underrepresented in a faculty or administrative unit, they will be given preferential consideration in cases of equal qualifications. To apply, please submit a CV, a list of publications, an overview of your research and teaching activities as well as transcripts and a selection of recent course evaluations online athttps://berufungsportal.uni-frankfurt.de by . If you have any questions, please contact Prof. Dr. Elisabeth Hollender at hollender@em.uni-frankfurt.de. Further information about the appointment process, the legal framework and data protection: www.professorship-vacancies.uni-frankfurt.de."
    },
    "https://berufungsportal.uni-frankfurt.de/application?procedure=872740C9-6799-F412-CC4E-83802F2F8488": {
      "title": "Professor (W3) of Maternal Health and Childbirth",
      "description": "  NICHT FREIGEBEN Medium  FREIGEBEN The Faculty of Medicine of the Goethe University Frankfurt am Main and the University Hospital Frankfurt, Institute for Midwifery Sciences invites applications for the following position as civil servant or public employee starting as soon as possible: Professor (W3) of Maternal Health and Childbirth The professorship is initially limited to a term of five years. Professorship Profile The professorship covers the field of Maternal Health and Childbirth within the joint degree program in Midwifery Science (B.Sc.). It operates in conjunction with existing professorships at the Frankfurt University of Applied Sciences dedicated to teaching and research in midwifery science and related disciplines. The position entails the directorship of an Institute for Midwifery Sciences and the responsibility for organizing and running the courses of the joint degree program in Midwifery Science (B.Sc.) at the Faculty of Medicine at Goethe University Frankfurt. Responsibilities related to patient care are governed by a service agreement—including performance-based wages—with Frankfurt University Hospital. We expect an exceptional pedagogical and didactic aptitude, as well as relevant experience in educating students in the areas of pregnancy and childbirth. Given the diverse cultural and ethical dimensions of the field, extensive transcultural experience is also highly desirable. Your Profile We are searching for an experienced professional capable of representing the full scope of the discipline across research, teaching, and patient care. Prerequisites for an appointment include a completed university degree in medicine or midwifery, a doctorate, a habilitation (or equivalent academic achievements), and an internationally recognized research profile evidenced by relevant publications, and in the case of a completed medical degree the board certification as a specialist in Gynecology and Obstetrics, extensive clinical experience, as well as additional relevant qualifications in the area of maternity protection and childbirth (e.g., specialized genetic counseling, DEGUM II certification in Gynecology and Obstetrics, IBCLC lactation consultancy, medical quality management). You possess extensive experience in teaching students and demonstrate a high level of commitment. Experience in management and personnel leadership is expected. You are also able to convincingly demonstrate how your work aligns with the research areas and collaborative projects of the Faculty of Medicine, Goethe University, and the Rhine-Main Universities (RMU). Experience in fostering early-career researchers, promoting gender equality, and supervising qualification theses is also desirable. Applicants are required to submit a structured document—not exceeding 10 pages—outlining forward-looking concepts for the professorship’s research, teaching, and clinical activities, based on their own experience and expertise. Requirements for Appointment The employment requirements as defined in § 68 of HessHG apply. Among other things, this includes proof of aptitude for academic work (e.g., a doctorate) and the subject-specific requirements listed under \"Your profile\" that are necessary for fulfilling the duties of the professorship. Your Application Goethe University and University Hospital Frankfurt are committed to equal opportunity, family friendliness, and diversity. To strengthen the diversity of perspectives and lived experiences within the university and the hospital, applications from indivi- duals with a migration background and from members of other groups that have so far been underrepresented are particularly welcome. Applicants with a severe disability, or those legally equivalent, will be given preferential consideration in cases of equal suitability. If women are underrepresented in a faculty or administrative unit, they will be given preferential consideration in cases of equal qualifications. To apply, please submit a CV, a list of publications, an overview of your research and teaching activities as well as transcripts and a selection of recent course evaluations online at https://berufungsportal.uni-frankfurt.de by 15.12.2026. Please direct any questions to the Dean´s office: dekan@med.uni-frankfurt.de. Further information about the appointment process, the legal framework and data protection: www.professorship-vacancies.uni-frankfurt.de. www.uni-frankfurt.de VorschauProfessor (W3)ofMaternal Healthand Childbirth JohannWolfgang Goethe-UniversitätFrankfurt | FrankfurtamMain"
    }
